// The demo scene, as a version 4 graph document. Nothing about this scene is
// set up in Rust: the camera, the light, the meshes and the materials are all
// nodes, and every connection below is an edge in this file.
//
//   midiTime ──time──▶ lfoA, lfoB
//   lfoA ──amplitude──▶ lfoB
//   lfoA ──y──▶ vec3A ──translation──▶ cubeA ─┐
//   lfoB ──y──▶ vec3B ──translation──▶ cubeB ─┤─children─▶ group
//   mat  ──material──▶ cubeA, cubeB, cubeC              │
//   cube ──mesh──────▶ cubeA, cubeB, cubeC ─────────────┘
//
// Geometry, material and placement are separate nodes (redesign-graph-model).
// What used to be one `cubeA` entity carrying `MeshAsset` *and* a `Transform`
// is now a producer node (`cube`, which owns the loaded mesh asset) plus three
// scene nodes (`cubeA`/`cubeB`/`cubeC`, which own a placement each). That is
// why there is exactly **one** `cube.gltf` reference in this file where the
// wire model had three: one mesh serves several placements, and the sharing is
// visible as three `cube.mesh -> …mesh` edges rather than three nodes naming
// the same path. The same split applies to the sprite layers below —
// `spritePlaneMesh`/`spritePlane` and `spritePlaneMesh2`/`spritePlane2`.
//
// `mesh` and `material` edges are **marker edges**: they carry no value (their
// port types are zero-sized), so nothing propagates along them. They exist to
// say *which* producer a placement reads and to order projection — the mesh
// exists before the placement asks for it.
//
// The cubes' x offsets live in the `MakeVec3` nodes because an edge writes
// `translation` whole. `cubeA`/`cubeB` therefore carry an identity pose in
// this file: their translation is driven, and an authored one would be
// overwritten on the first tick anyway.
//
// `cubeC` is the odd one out: an authored pose and no translation edge,
// on purpose (M7 Task 15's exit-criterion walkthrough needs one mesh whose
// drag actually holds — cubeA/cubeB's translate handle springs back on the
// next tick by design, M7-7, which makes them useless for proving a
// translate-drag "sticks").
//
// Below the cube group sits a second content kind: two sprite layers, added
// for add-sprite-material. Same conventions, same `midiTime`, no new kind of
// node to learn:
//
//   midiTime ────time─────▶ spriteOsc, spriteOsc2
//   spriteOsc ───input────▶ spriteRemap ───frame───▶ spriteMat ─┐
//   spriteOsc2 ──input────▶ spriteRemap2 ──frame───▶ spriteMat2 ┤
//   colorSeq ───color─────▶ spriteMat, spriteMat2               │
//   depthSeq ───depth─────▶ spriteMat, spriteMat2               │
//   spriteMat ───material─▶ spritePlane                         │
//   spriteMat2 ──material─▶ spritePlane2 ◀─────────────────────┘
//
// `frame` is never authored and never a bespoke animation node — design
// D3/D4's whole point. It is three nodes that already exist: `MidiTime` (the
// same node the cubes' LFOs read) feeds an `Oscillator` running `Saw`, whose
// -1..1 output `Remap` rescales to 0..30, the sequence's frame count. Nobody
// clamps on the write side: the sprite material's read-side `layer_index` is
// what keeps a `Remap` output that reaches exactly 30.0 on frame 29 rather
// than sampling out of range (D4) — spriteRemap's `out_max: 30.0` is
// deliberately exact, not `29.0`, to let that safeguard do its job. The two
// layers run the same period but opposite phase (`spriteOsc2.phase: 0.5`),
// so they are never on the same frame — a visible "own frame offset" per
// layer without a second animation mechanism.
//
// `colorSeq` and `depthSeq` are each connected to *both* materials — one
// `FrameSequence` loading a folder once and feeding two consumers is D7's
// "one sequence serves many consumers" scenario, proved by sharing rather
// than asserted.
//
// Depth sign: the sprite assets' own convention is 0.0 = nearest the camera,
// 1.0 = farthest (`sprite_material.wgsl`'s header). The shader's vertex stage
// displaces `+world_normal * (height - depth_pivot) * depth_range` — its own
// comment calls this "standard displacement-map convention: a value above
// the pivot pushes out along the normal", and flags that as the *opposite*
// sign to the asset convention above, which was authored to the older M8
// spike's "higher = farther from camera" rule. Both sprite planes face the
// camera near enough to treat their local +Z as "toward camera" (spritePlane
// exactly; spritePlane2 within its 30° yaw), so a positive `depth_range`
// would push the brighter, farther pixels *toward* the camera and the
// darker, nearer pixels *away* from it — backwards. `depth_range` is
// therefore authored negative on both layers, which restores the intended
// reading without touching the shader or the assets.
//
// spritePlane's placement is chosen to interpenetrate `cubeC`
// (`translation: (0.0, 1.6, -0.8)`, half-extent 1.0, so
// x ∈ [-1, 1], y ∈ [0.6, 2.6], z ∈ [-1.8, 0.2]). With `depth_pivot: 0.5` and
// the measured relief 0.158..0.889 (see add-sprite-material's task-3.1 notes),
// max displacement is `(0.889 - 0.5) * 3.75 ≈ 1.459` one way and
// `(0.5 - 0.158) * 3.75 ≈ 1.283` the other. spritePlane sits at
// `(0.0, 1.6, -0.6)`, unrotated (local +Z ≈ world +Z ≈ toward the camera), so
// its relief spans world z ∈ [-0.6 - 1.459, -0.6 + 1.283] = [-2.06, 0.68] —
// which fully contains cubeC's z ∈ [-1.8, 0.2] — while its 1.4×1.4 footprint
// (x ∈ [-0.7, 0.7], y ∈ [0.9, 2.3]) sits entirely inside cubeC's x/y
// cross-section. The relief therefore passes all the way through the cube,
// not just grazes it.
//
// spritePlane2 overlaps spritePlane (base (0.3, 1.5, -0.5), size 1.2×1.2,
// its own `depth_range: -3.5`) and carries a 30° yaw about Y
// (`rotation: (0.0, 0.258819, 0.0, 0.965926)`), so its relief's displacement
// axis is not parallel to spritePlane's — the two reliefs interleave rather
// than sitting as parallel sheets, which is what makes both "two sprite
// layers interpenetrate" and (add-sprite-material task 4.2) the parallax
// check reachable by eye. The plane geometry is authored on its own
// `PlaneMesh` producer node; `size` is the quad, and its default 63×63
// tessellation is what the displacement has to work with.
//
// Format notes: `type` is a node kind's *short* name, resolved against the
// type registry at load, so moving a node kind between modules cannot break
// this file. `inlets` holds authored inlets only — never `state` (handles,
// loaded paths, oscillator memory) and never `outlets`; both come from the
// kind's own defaults. `metadata` holds annotations the document carries and
// does not interpret: each value records its own type path, so no key has a
// field of its own and nothing here declares what `"pos"` means — that is the
// editor's canvas placement, and the editor is the only thing that reads it.
// An edge names two part-relative paths and a slot: the
// source path is inside the producer's `outlets`, the destination path inside
// the consumer's `inlets`, and `slot` is a sort key, used only where several
// edges land on one variadic inlet (here: `group.children`, at 10/20/30, so a
// fourth cube can be inserted between two of them without renumbering).
Graph(
    version: 4,
    nodes: {
        // ---------------------------------------------------------------
        // Time, and the two cube LFOs.
        // ---------------------------------------------------------------
        "midiTime": Node(type: "MidiTime", metadata: {"pos": {"glam::Vec2": (-700.0, 100.0)}}, inlets: ()),
        "lfoA": Node(type: "Oscillator", metadata: {"pos": {"glam::Vec2": (-460.0, 40.0)}}, inlets: (time: 0.0, period: 8.0, shape: Sine, phase: 0.0, amplitude: 0.5)),
        "lfoB": Node(type: "Oscillator", metadata: {"pos": {"glam::Vec2": (-460.0, 160.0)}}, inlets: (time: 0.0, period: 2.0, shape: Sine, phase: 0.0, amplitude: 0.0)),
        "vec3A": Node(type: "MakeVec3", metadata: {"pos": {"glam::Vec2": (-220.0, 40.0)}}, inlets: (x: -0.8, y: 0.0, z: 0.0)),
        "vec3B": Node(type: "MakeVec3", metadata: {"pos": {"glam::Vec2": (-220.0, 160.0)}}, inlets: (x: 0.8, y: 0.0, z: 0.0)),

        // ---------------------------------------------------------------
        // The cubes: one mesh producer, one material producer, three
        // placements, one group.
        // ---------------------------------------------------------------
        "cube": Node(type: "MeshAsset", metadata: {"pos": {"glam::Vec2": (20.0, -80.0)}}, inlets: (path: "cube.gltf#Mesh0/Primitive0")),
        "mat": Node(type: "PbrMaterial", metadata: {"pos": {"glam::Vec2": (180.0, 260.0)}}, inlets: (base_color: (0.6, 0.7, 0.9), metallic: 0.1, roughness: 0.4)),
        "cubeA": Node(type: "MeshNode", metadata: {"pos": {"glam::Vec2": (20.0, 40.0)}}, inlets: (translation: (0.0, 0.0, 0.0), rotation: (0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0), scale: (1.0, 1.0, 1.0))),
        "cubeB": Node(type: "MeshNode", metadata: {"pos": {"glam::Vec2": (20.0, 160.0)}}, inlets: (translation: (0.0, 0.0, 0.0), rotation: (0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0), scale: (1.0, 1.0, 1.0))),
        "cubeC": Node(type: "MeshNode", metadata: {"pos": {"glam::Vec2": (20.0, 280.0)}}, inlets: (translation: (0.0, 1.6, -0.8), rotation: (0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0), scale: (1.0, 1.0, 1.0))),
        "group": Node(type: "Group", metadata: {"pos": {"glam::Vec2": (260.0, 100.0)}}, inlets: (translation: (0.0, 0.0, 0.0), rotation: (0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0), scale: (1.0, 1.0, 1.0))),

        // ---------------------------------------------------------------
        // What looks at the scene, and what lights it.
        // ---------------------------------------------------------------
        "camera": Node(type: "Camera", metadata: {"pos": {"glam::Vec2": (420.0, -120.0)}}, inlets: (translation: (0.0, 1.5, 5.0), rotation: (-0.14521316, 0.0, 0.0, 0.98940045), scale: (1.0, 1.0, 1.0))),
        "sun": Node(type: "DirectionalLight", metadata: {"pos": {"glam::Vec2": (420.0, -20.0)}}, inlets: (translation: (4.0, 8.0, 4.0), rotation: (-0.424708, 0.339851, 0.175920, 0.820473), scale: (1.0, 1.0, 1.0), illuminance: 6000.0)),
        // What the window and the HDMI path present. Without this, a document
        // with a camera presents nothing: which camera is shown is authored,
        // never guessed from creation order or from whichever rendered last.
        // The camera's own `resolution` is left at its 1920x1080 default,
        // which is why this entry does not name it.
        "output": Node(type: "Output", metadata: {"pos": {"glam::Vec2": (640.0, -120.0)}}, inlets: ()),

        // ---------------------------------------------------------------
        // Sprite layers (add-sprite-material). See the header diagram and
        // the depth-sign / interpenetration arithmetic above.
        // ---------------------------------------------------------------
        "colorSeq": Node(type: "FrameSequence", metadata: {"pos": {"glam::Vec2": (-220.0, 480.0)}}, inlets: (folder: "sprites/pulse_color", color_space: Display)),
        // Data, not Display: this run is heights, not colour, and reading it
        // through an sRGB view would warp every displacement (design D8).
        "depthSeq": Node(type: "FrameSequence", metadata: {"pos": {"glam::Vec2": (-220.0, 540.0)}}, inlets: (folder: "sprites/pulse_depth", color_space: Data)),
        "spriteOsc": Node(type: "Oscillator", metadata: {"pos": {"glam::Vec2": (-460.0, 420.0)}}, inlets: (time: 0.0, period: 6.0, shape: Saw, phase: 0.0, amplitude: 1.0)),
        // Same period, opposite phase: the two layers are always on different
        // frames without a second animation mechanism.
        "spriteOsc2": Node(type: "Oscillator", metadata: {"pos": {"glam::Vec2": (-460.0, 620.0)}}, inlets: (time: 0.0, period: 6.0, shape: Saw, phase: 0.5, amplitude: 1.0)),
        // -1..1 (Saw's own range) to 0..30 (the sequence's 30 frames).
        // out_max is exactly 30.0 on purpose — the read-side clamp is what
        // turns a value that reaches it into layer 29, not a `29.0` authored
        // here to dodge that.
        "spriteRemap": Node(type: "Remap", metadata: {"pos": {"glam::Vec2": (-220.0, 420.0)}}, inlets: (in_min: -1.0, in_max: 1.0, out_min: 0.0, out_max: 30.0, clamp: false)),
        "spriteRemap2": Node(type: "Remap", metadata: {"pos": {"glam::Vec2": (-220.0, 620.0)}}, inlets: (in_min: -1.0, in_max: 1.0, out_min: 0.0, out_max: 30.0, clamp: false)),
        // depth_range negative: see the header's depth-sign note.
        "spriteMat": Node(type: "SpriteMaterial", metadata: {"pos": {"glam::Vec2": (20.0, 420.0)}}, inlets: (depth_range: -3.75, depth_pivot: 0.5)),
        // A tint (own colour) and its own depth_range, both authored rather
        // than driven — nothing here says a material's per-layer knobs must
        // be graph-driven, only that frame timing is (D3/D4).
        "spriteMat2": Node(type: "SpriteMaterial", metadata: {"pos": {"glam::Vec2": (20.0, 620.0)}}, inlets: (tint: (1.0, 0.82, 0.86), depth_range: -3.5, depth_pivot: 0.5)),
        "spritePlaneMesh": Node(type: "PlaneMesh", metadata: {"pos": {"glam::Vec2": (180.0, 360.0)}}, inlets: (size: (1.4, 1.4))),
        "spritePlaneMesh2": Node(type: "PlaneMesh", metadata: {"pos": {"glam::Vec2": (180.0, 560.0)}}, inlets: (size: (1.2, 1.2))),
        // Authored poses, no translation edge, like cubeC — these
        // placements are static, chosen to interpenetrate cubeC and each
        // other (see the header's arithmetic).
        "spritePlane": Node(type: "MeshNode", metadata: {"pos": {"glam::Vec2": (260.0, 420.0)}}, inlets: (translation: (0.0, 1.6, -0.6), rotation: (0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0), scale: (1.0, 1.0, 1.0))),
        // 30° yaw about Y — a non-trivial authored rotation, so its relief's
        // displacement axis is not parallel to spritePlane's.
        "spritePlane2": Node(type: "MeshNode", metadata: {"pos": {"glam::Vec2": (260.0, 620.0)}}, inlets: (translation: (0.3, 1.5, -0.5), rotation: (0.0, 0.258819, 0.0, 0.965926), scale: (1.0, 1.0, 1.0))),
    },
    edges: [
        // Time into every oscillator.
        Edge(from: ("midiTime", "out"), to: ("lfoA", "time"), slot: 0),
        Edge(from: ("midiTime", "out"), to: ("lfoB", "time"), slot: 0),
        Edge(from: ("midiTime", "out"), to: ("spriteOsc", "time"), slot: 0),
        Edge(from: ("midiTime", "out"), to: ("spriteOsc2", "time"), slot: 0),
        // lfoA both drives cubeA and modulates lfoB's amplitude.
        Edge(from: ("lfoA", "out"), to: ("lfoB", "amplitude"), slot: 0),
        Edge(from: ("lfoA", "out"), to: ("vec3A", "y"), slot: 0),
        Edge(from: ("lfoB", "out"), to: ("vec3B", "y"), slot: 0),
        // A whole Vec3 into a placement's translation.
        Edge(from: ("vec3A", "out"), to: ("cubeA", "translation"), slot: 0),
        Edge(from: ("vec3B", "out"), to: ("cubeB", "translation"), slot: 0),
        // The camera into the output node. A marker edge like the ones below:
        // it carries identity only, and no image travels along it.
        Edge(from: ("camera", "camera"), to: ("output", "camera"), slot: 0),
        // One mesh, three placements. Marker edges: no value flows.
        Edge(from: ("cube", "mesh"), to: ("cubeA", "mesh"), slot: 0),
        Edge(from: ("cube", "mesh"), to: ("cubeB", "mesh"), slot: 0),
        Edge(from: ("cube", "mesh"), to: ("cubeC", "mesh"), slot: 0),
        // One material, the same three placements.
        Edge(from: ("mat", "material"), to: ("cubeA", "material"), slot: 0),
        Edge(from: ("mat", "material"), to: ("cubeB", "material"), slot: 0),
        Edge(from: ("mat", "material"), to: ("cubeC", "material"), slot: 0),
        // The hierarchy. `children` is variadic, so the slots are the order,
        // spaced out so a fourth cube can be inserted without renumbering.
        Edge(from: ("cubeA", "child"), to: ("group", "children"), slot: 10),
        Edge(from: ("cubeB", "child"), to: ("group", "children"), slot: 20),
        Edge(from: ("cubeC", "child"), to: ("group", "children"), slot: 30),
        // The sprite layers' frame numbers.
        Edge(from: ("spriteOsc", "out"), to: ("spriteRemap", "input"), slot: 0),
        Edge(from: ("spriteOsc2", "out"), to: ("spriteRemap2", "input"), slot: 0),
        Edge(from: ("spriteRemap", "out"), to: ("spriteMat", "frame"), slot: 0),
        Edge(from: ("spriteRemap2", "out"), to: ("spriteMat2", "frame"), slot: 0),
        // One colour run and one depth run, each feeding both materials.
        Edge(from: ("colorSeq", "sequence"), to: ("spriteMat", "color"), slot: 0),
        Edge(from: ("colorSeq", "sequence"), to: ("spriteMat2", "color"), slot: 0),
        Edge(from: ("depthSeq", "sequence"), to: ("spriteMat", "depth"), slot: 0),
        Edge(from: ("depthSeq", "sequence"), to: ("spriteMat2", "depth"), slot: 0),
        // Geometry and material onto each sprite placement.
        Edge(from: ("spritePlaneMesh", "mesh"), to: ("spritePlane", "mesh"), slot: 0),
        Edge(from: ("spritePlaneMesh2", "mesh"), to: ("spritePlane2", "mesh"), slot: 0),
        Edge(from: ("spriteMat", "material"), to: ("spritePlane", "material"), slot: 0),
        Edge(from: ("spriteMat2", "material"), to: ("spritePlane2", "material"), slot: 0),
    ],
)
